# epaper-linux-x86_64

The generic hosted x86-64 board with its MCU and screen pointed at the
emulated SSD1680. Everything else is inherited: the same SDK, the same named
device map, and the same RTC and IMU providers.

Rebinding mm.mcu, not only mm.display, is what makes the window real: the
emulated chip sits behind the same seam the real driver talks to, and the
SDL2 window is owned by that MCU provider. Selecting this board is the only
way anything in the e-paper lane pays for SDL2.
